title: Widgets

HyperGSD uses custom wikitext widgets to drive behaviour. All are defined in `$:/plugins/yan/hypergsd/modules/widgets/`, and called with the standard TiddlyWiki element syntax `<$widget>`. Most carry the `$:/tags/Global` tag (resolvable everywhere); `$hgsd.list` and `$hgsd.convert` are `$:/tags/Global/View` (ViewTemplate subtree + edit preview only — anything reachable from a modal must stay Global).

! HyperGSD Widgets

;[[$hgsd.list|hgsd.list widget]]
:Realm-aware, refresh-frozen list engine used by every dashboard. See its own page for the full parameter table and examples.

;[[<$hgsd.toggle>|$:/plugins/yan/hypergsd/modules/widgets/hgsd-toggle]]
:Disclosure wrapper: children render behind a show/hide button pair over the standard reveal idiom. Default state is per hosting page (`$:/state/hypergsd/show-completed/<page>`, shared by members using the default together); `state`/`state-prefix`/`class` override, and `unwrap-tag-lists` renders children bare when the member is a tag's whole content (the dedicated Completed pages). Used by the dashboard completed lists and the project view's completed member.

;[[<$hgsd.convert>|hgsd.convert widget]]
:Convert the current Action tiddler into a Project tiddler.

;[[<$hgsd.new-button>|hgsd.new-button widget]]
:Opens the new-item modal pre-seeded with type, status, project, contact, context and realm parameters.

;[[<$hgsd.realm-picker>|hgsd.realm-picker widget]]
:Plain realm select bound to a state tiddler — sub-plugin-facing convenience for "pick a realm into my state".

;[[<$hgsd.pick>|hgsd.pick widget]]
:Searchable popup listbox picker with realm scoping — writes single-value fields, or appends to list fields via the instant-commit parameters.

;[[<$hgsd.pick-field>|hgsd.pick-field widget]]
:Three-state field editor (empty/set/editing) wrapping `<$hgsd.pick>`; the `tiddler` parameter names the write target (blank = the current tiddler — the modal points it at its working temp).

;[[<$hgsd.pick-append>|hgsd.pick-append widget]]
:One-row list adder wrapping `<$hgsd.pick>` — the pick family's list member; `direction` picks the write side ("own" appends the pick to the target's field, "item" appends the target's title to the picked tiddler's field).

;[[<$refresh>|$refresh widget]]
:Freezes a region against the global refresh cycle; only tiddlers matching a whitelist re-render it.

For the non-widget globals (`hgsd-item`, `hgsd-render-inner`, `hgsd-handle-click`, `hgsd-type-gate`, the status-radio and picker procedures), see [[API Procedures|Procedures and Globals]].